// R1's two-direction controls. The acceptance condition for R1 is that a fix moves BOTH error
// directions, because the measured defect is ONE inconsistency producing opposite signs — a
// producer's Rc<T> reaching a bare consumer over-wraps, a bare producer reaching an Rc<T> consumer
// under-wraps — so a control drawn from one direction alone cannot distinguish the right fix from
// the position-based fix that moves half the population and worsens the other half. Both
// directions are drawn from the LIVE rust catalog rather than a synthetic fixture, by varying only
// the flow's direction over one carrier whose rows already disagree by position: Diagnostics is
// ReferenceLayerRc at OwnershipAtBindingProjection and ReferenceLayerOwned at
// OwnershipAtFunctionParameter, so binding-to-param is the over shape and param-to-binding is the
// under shape. wrap_decision_flow_gate must refuse BOTH; today's per-position gate accepts both
// and emits the producer's layer, which is the silent wrongness. The layer-discrimination control
// is the one that keeps wrap_decisions_equal honest: Node is ReferenceLayerRc at binding and
// ReferenceLayerBox at struct field, two DIFFERENT reference layers, and an implementation
// comparing only by-value against by-reference would call that agreement and pass every other
// control here. RED, executed rather than asserted, and the profile is reported exactly as
// measured because it is not uniform. Mutation one, wrap_decision_gates_agree forced to true: the
// over-wrap, under-wrap and distinct-layer witnesses all go RED; the missing-row witness and both
// accept witnesses stay GREEN. So the missing-row witness does NOT discriminate this
// reconciliation — it is a regression control proving an underlying catalog miss still propagates
// through the flow gate rather than being swallowed by it, and saying it discriminates
// disagreement would be inflation. Mutation two, wrap_decisions_equal made layer-blind so any two
// WrapByReference count as equal: ONLY the distinct-layer witness goes RED, which is what earns
// that witness its place — Rc against Box is a real disagreement that a by-value-versus-by-
// reference comparison calls agreement, and every other witness here passes under that bug. The
// agreement and inapplicable witnesses are the positive controls that stop a refuse-always
// implementation from earning a degenerate pass on the refusal half.
fn wrap_decision_flow_rejects(
  target: v2.std.compilers.target_model.TargetModel,
  source_carrier: v2.std.node.Node,
  producer_site: v2.std.compilers.target_model.TargetOwnershipUseSite,
  consumer_site: v2.std.compilers.target_model.TargetOwnershipUseSite
) -> Bool {
  match v2.compiler.wrap_decision.wrap_decision_flow_gate(
    target: target,
    source_carrier: source_carrier,
    producer_site: producer_site,
    consumer_site: consumer_site
  ) {
    v2.std.diagnostic.Rejected { diagnostics: _ } => true
    v2.std.diagnostic.Accepted { value: _, diagnostics: _ } => false
  }
}

